      "source_line_start": 1076,
      "source_line_end": 1087,
      "current_tex": "\\begin{theorem}[Supremum of a Sum Set]\n\\label{thm:supremum-sum-set}\nLet $A,B\\subseteq\\mathbb{R}$ be nonempty and bounded above.  Then\n$A+B:=\\{a+b:a\\in A,\\ b\\in B\\}$ is nonempty and bounded above, and\n\\[\n  \\sup(A+B)=\\sup A+\\sup B.\n\\]\n\n\\smallskip\n\\noindent\n\\hyperref[prf:supremum-sum-set]{\\textit{Go to proof.}}\n\\end{theorem}",
